# libp2p (ADR 0019)

TCP+TLS remains the industrial default. libp2p is opt-in `FEATURE_LIBP2P` / `feature_libp2p=false` in prod JSON. Experimental sandbox only — never flip audit-pin / `v1.3.1339-tip-v2-industrial`.

## Slice claims

ADR text on disk is the source of truth (slices continue past BM/BN). **Do not** hardcode a phase number (e.g. "65 of 76") in status or docs. Read `docs/adr/0019-rust-libp2p-industrial.md` and **never claim a slice complete** without:

```powershell
.\scripts\verify_adr0019_libp2p_hard.ps1
```

Lab PASS with `FEATURE_LIBP2P=true` does **not** authorize industrial compose.

## After changes

1. Run the hard verify script (not only the soft/Python lab).
2. Document the new slice in ADR 0019 (table + status).
3. Keep Absolute wire as protocol-on-streams; do not replace TCP+TLS by accident.
